{
  "id": "freecad_cw_part_060",
  "app": "freecad",
  "task": "Create a combined Part model. Start with a Part box sized 50 mm along global X, 30 mm along global Y, and 10 mm along global Z, with its lower-back-left corner at the origin so it spans X = 0 to 50, Y = 0 to 30, and Z = 0 to 10. Create a solid Part cylinder with radius 10 mm and height 10 mm, axis along global Z, centered at X = 50, Y = 15, and spanning Z = 0 to 10, so it is fused to the right side of the box and protrudes from X = 40 to 60. Fuse the box and cylinder into one solid. Then cut a 6 mm radius through-hole using a second cylinder coaxial with the added cylinder, centered at X = 50, Y = 15, axis along global Z, passing completely through the fused solid. Build it as a Part Box, a Part Union (Part::MultiFuse) of the box and the first cylinder, and a Part Cut of that union by the second cylinder, keeping FreeCAD's default names: box label 'Cube', cylinders named 'Cylinder' (the added one) and 'Cylinder001' (the hole), union label 'Fusion', cut label 'Cut'. Save the completed model to /home/user/Unnamed.FCStd.",
  "env": {
    "files": []
  },
